= Overfitting — Simple =

'''Overfitting''' happens when a machine-learning system learns details of its training or development data that do not help on new data.

It may look excellent during training but perform worse when tested independently.

A large model is not automatically overfit.

Modern models can have huge numbers of parameters and still generalize well.

Overfitting is diagnosed by how the learning process performs on new data, not by size alone.

